      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Histamine is an important mediator and regulator of inflammation. Histamine acts via H1, H2, and H3 receptors that are functionally coupled to G-proteins and histamine release is regulated by cytokines that act as histamine release factors. Histamine suppresses the immune response and deviates the immune response toward the Th2 pathway."},
